"""Present the exact N18 AC5 witness and maximal subspace dimension."""
from pathlib import Path
import html,json,re
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;ROOT=HERE.parents[1]
def m(x,display=True):
 tag='div' if display else 'span';return f'<{tag} class="math" data-display="{str(display).lower()}" data-tex="{html.escape(x,quote=True)}"></{tag}>'
def links(items):return '<div class="proof-links">'+''.join(f'<a href="{html.escape(u,quote=True)}">{t} ↗</a>' for u,t in items)+'</div>'
def main():
 r=json.loads((HERE/'verification.json').read_text());assert r['passed'] and r['maximumDimension']==1
 css=re.search(r'<style>(.*?)</style>',(ROOT/'research/t2-qec-upper/index.html').read_text(),re.S).group(1)+'\n.math{max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto}.badge{color:#1c6253;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.08em}'
 b='<p class="eyebrow">Anticoherent states and subspaces · Exact witness and optimal dimension</p><a href="../../index.html#n=18&t=5">← Catalogue entry</a><h1>Eighteen qubits: fifth order is attained</h1>'
 b+='<div class="result"><span class="badge">Proved · arbitrary complex subspaces</span>'+m(r'\boxed{K(18,5)=1.}')+'<p>The exact state already present in the AC-state catalogue supplies the lower bound. Rectangular tensor images exclude a two-dimensional fifth-order subspace.</p></div>'
 b+='<section><h2>The existing analytical state</h2>'+m(r'\begin{aligned}\sqrt{130}|\psi\rangle&=\sqrt{14}\bigl(|D_{18}^{(0)}\rangle+|D_{18}^{(18)}\rangle\bigr)\\&\quad+i\sqrt{51}\bigl(|D_{18}^{(5)}\rangle+|D_{18}^{(13)}\rangle\bigr).\end{aligned}')+'<p>The supplied Julia source gives this same ray at line 203 and credits M. Grassl. The expression above simplifies its normalized coefficients; it is not a newly discovered representative.</p>'+links([('../../../anticoherent-state-catalogue/index.html#n=18&t=5','Pure AC-state catalogue'),('../../index.html#n=18&t=5&subspace=line-acliege-n18-t5','Dicke coefficients and Majorana representation'),('../../references/ACLiege.jl','Supplied Julia source')])+'</section>'
 b+='<section><h2>Why the state is fifth-order AC</h2><p>The probabilities are '+m(r'14/130',False)+' at magnetic numbers '+m(r'm=\pm9',False)+' and '+m(r'51/130',False)+' at '+m(r'm=\pm4',False)+'. Their sum is one. Reflection symmetry cancels the odd moments, while</p>'+m(r'\langle J_z^2\rangle=30,\qquad\langle J_z^4\rangle=1614.')+'<p>These equal the normalized spin-nine traces. The support gaps eliminate every magnetic shift from one through four. At shift five, only the pairs '+m(r'0\to5',False)+' and '+m(r'13\to18',False)+' contribute. Their ladder factors are equal and their amplitude products have opposite signs, giving '+m(r'\langle J_+^5\rangle=0',False)+'. This covers every multipole through rank five.</p>'+m(r'\rho_5=I_6/6,\qquad\left\|\rho_6-I_7/7\right\|_F^2=\frac{73}{59150}.')+'<p>An independent standard-library verifier checks all 90 reduced-matrix entries through order five, the sixth-order residual and association with the source coefficients. The residual describes this particular state; a separate proof excludes all other sixth-order candidates.</p></section>'
 b+='<section><h2>Why the maximum dimension is one</h2><p>For a fifth-order AC subspace with orthonormal basis '+m(r'u_1,\ldots,u_k',False)+', take complete Hilbert–Schmidt orthonormal rectangular tensor multiplets</p>'+m(r'E_{\ell q}:V_9\longrightarrow V_{17/2},\qquad\ell=\tfrac12,\tfrac32,\tfrac52.')+'<p>There are '+m(r'2+4+6=12',False)+' maps. Their pairwise products have ranks at most five. Polarizing the whole-subspace AC conditions therefore gives</p>'+m(r'\langle E_{\ell q}u_a,E_{\ell^{\prime}q^{\prime}}u_b\rangle=\frac{\delta_{ab}\delta_{\ell\ell^{\prime}}\delta_{qq^{\prime}}}{19}.')+'<p>These '+m(r'12k',False)+' nonzero orthogonal vectors must fit in the eighteen-dimensional output space:</p>'+m(r'12k\le18\quad\Longrightarrow\quad k\le1.')+'<p>The displayed state attains the bound. No support or reality assumption is imposed on the excluded subspaces.</p>'+links([('proof.tex','Complete LaTeX proof'),('verify.py','Independent exact witness verifier'),('verification.json','Successful exact verification')])+'</section>'
 b+='<section><h2>The maximum pure-state order is also five</h2><p>A separate exact three-copy positivity identity excludes every sixth-order state on eighteen qubits. Thus</p>'+m(r'\boxed{t_{\max}(18)=5,\qquad K(18,t)=0\quad(t\ge6).}')+links([('../n18-t6/index.html','Sixth-order nonexistence proof')])+'</section>'
 head='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>N=18: fifth-order AC dimension one</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script defer src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js"></script><style>'+css+'</style><script>document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",()=>document.querySelectorAll("[data-tex]").forEach(el=>{if(window.katex)el.innerHTML=katex.renderToString(el.dataset.tex,{displayMode:el.dataset.display==="true",throwOnError:false,strict:"ignore",trust:false});}));</script></head><body><main>'
 (HERE/'index.html').write_text(head+b+'</main></body></html>\n')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
